(D4 - Discrepancy 4 repro: a number flag given a value past the range of a
 number. Up to vox 0.4.15 it set the error flag AND left a wrapped value
 behind (99999999999999999999 - 5 * 2^64 = 7766279631452241919), and this
 probe printed "retries is 7766279631452241919" then "and it computes:
 -2914184810805067778".
 RESOLVED by vox #281: the token is not a number (LANGUAGE.md:2233-2235),
 so the flag holds its default, 0, and the error flag is raised
 (LANGUAGE.md:4926-4928). Re-recorded 2026-10-13 on vox main a0a2ecc.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D4.vox -o p && ./p -r 99999999999999999999
 Args: -r 99999999999999999999
 expected output:
   retries is 0
   and it computes: 0
)
a flag called retries is "-r" or "--retries", it is a number.
Parse flags.

Print "retries is {retries}".
a number called doubled is retries multiply 2.
